id: pm-gh1611
title: "GH-1611: render portable tracker scope in generated completion hints"
description: "GitHub report https://github.com/unbraind/pm-cli/issues/1611 shows pm close completion guidance serializing the resolved absolute tracker root even for the default cwd tracker. Investigate portable scope rendering across generated hints while preserving an explicitly selected tracker and extension mode. Independently reproduced on pinned original source. Current shared SDK scope formatter preserves explicit selection and extension mode, omits implicit defaults, and renders distinct environment roots relative to the invocation. Two-tracker shell replay and full exact coverage pass; hosted admission and revised-head review remain required. Completed lifecycle-example explicit-scope preservation remains completed."
type: Issue
status: in_progress
priority: 2
tags[2]: agent-ux,github
created_at: "2026-10-27T10:20:17.530Z"
updated_at: "2026-10-27T17:44:23.279Z"
assignee: "harness:codex"
claim_principal: "harness:codex#4f9b0131c245b9f712c46790"
author: "harness:codex"
estimated_minutes: 120
acceptance_criteria: Reproduce completion hint behavior in isolated cwd-default and explicitly selected trackers; preserve caller-provided relative scope and no-extensions mode; copied mutation examples target the selected tracker and leave ambient tracker bytes unchanged; cover shared hint formatting through SDK and thin CLI rendering without exposing host paths unnecessarily.
value: Keep copied guidance portable and avoid redundant host coordinates
impact: Generated completion hints and recovery examples consumed by agents
parent: pm-mpbb
risk: medium
confidence: medium
expected_result: Generated hints omit redundant default absolute roots and preserve explicit or distinct tracker selection through portable structured context.
